    {
      "text": "\n1. **Difference b/w client mode and cluster mode ?**\n  - Ans: spark support two deployemnt mode client mode where driver process runs on client machine, untill all executor process completed on master\n    - problem: network latency, clien die spark process die\n\n2. **What is partition skew, reasons for it. How to solve parition skew issues?**\n  - Ans: spark to execute the task in parallel , data divided in chunk , when we do any kind of aggregation based on some key, and that key has lot of data  , that cause unequal size of shuffle parition \n  that may not fit on single task. called data skewed\n     - solution:  \n        - Salting:  smalldf.withColumn(\"salt\", expload(lit((1 to 3).toArray)).join(largedf.withColumn(\"salt\", lit(f.rand*3))  , Seq(\"key\",\"salt\"), \"inner\")\n        - AQE:  spark.sql.adaptive.enabled=true\n\n3. ",
