    {
      "text": "### Lost executor problem\n\n executors being lost no matter how much memory we allocated to them.\n\n- The solution if you're using yarn was to\n- --conf spark.yarn.executor.memoryOverhead=600,\n- Resource manager launches containers in order to execute executors inside it. so basically executor memory + memory overhead = container memory\n\n- Executor memory overhead mainly includes off-heap memory and nio buffers and memory for running container-specific threads(thread stacks). when you do not specify memory overhead, Resource manager calculates memory overhead value by using default values and launch containers accordingly.\n\nIt is always recommended to keep aside cores and memory for OS (which is 1 core for nodemanager and 1 core for other daemons and 2 cores for OS to work optimally)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "0673c18422914836af319"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nspark.conf.get(\"spark.sql.files.maxParitionBytes\")\nspark.conf.get(\"spark.sql.files.maxRecordsPerFiles\")\nspark.conf.get(\"spark.sql.shuffle.paritions\")\n// spark.conf.get(\"\")",
      "config": {
