    {
      "text": "\n7. **If your spark is running slow, how wourld you approach to debug it**\n- Ans:\n     - i will check spark-ui for that job, will see which stage/task is taking time and why?\n      this might be due to skewed paritions, or might be due to slow netework i/o\n     - optimize join strategy\n     - increase no of executor and memory, to avoid iteration of task\n     - verify no of parition/shuffle partition during exchange\n     - metigate GC by givinf some offheap memory\n     - implement caching\n     - use parquet\n\n\n\n8.  **Why we are not using mapreduce these days, that are similarities b/w spark and mapreduce ?**\n- Ans:  mapreduce and spark both used to process data analytics workload, but in case of mapreduce , processed data is written to disk before reduce star on the same.\nbut in case of spark, spark is able to pipline the o/p to next task in memory \n\n\n9. **Explain about the cicd process?**\n -- feature/master, feture/dev, feature/release , feature/bugfix\n\n\n10. \n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
