      "id": "3a6602e07da24164a4b24"
    },
    {
      "text": "\n### Executor timeout\n\n\nprob: Spark cluster full of heartbeat timeouts, executors exiting on their own\n\n```Error:\n6 ERROR TransportChannelHandler: Connection to /10.0.0.4:35328 has been quiet for 120000 ms while there are outstanding requests. Assuming connection is dead; please adjust spark.network.timeout if this is wrong.\n16/05/16 10:11:26 ERROR CoarseGrainedExecutorBackend: Cannot register with driver: spark://CoarseGrainedScheduler@10.0.0.4:35328\n```\n\n**Solution**\n\n1. executors being killed by YARN is nearly always due to OOMs. You should inspect the logs on the individual executors (look for the text \"running beyond physical memory\"). or repartition you data\n\n2.  increase timeout time\n```\n(Note all mentioned time are in ms) and heartbeatInterval (default 10000) should be lesser than the timeout (default 120000)\n\nconf = SparkConf().setAppName(\"applicaiton\") \\\n.set(\"spark.executor.heartbeatInterval\", \"200000\") \\ \n.set(\"spark.network.timeout\", \"300000\")\nsc = SparkContext.getOrCreate(conf)\nsqlcontext = SQLContext(sc)\n```",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "8da35a7cc5da4adba61c7"
    },
