    {
      "text": "\n3. **What is broadcast join(Map side join) in apache spark?**\n- Ans: spark has a property call autobroadcastjointhreshhold which is default to 10mb , when we join a large data sets with samller datasets, if small r data set is below threhhold , then spark \nexchange broadcast the smaller dataset to each executor, to reduce the network i/o and shuffle read and perform broadcast has join on each paritions\n\n4. **what is diff b/w parition and bucketing?**\n- Ans: \n  - parition: column which has low cardinality dataset can be paritioned and saved to hdfs , if the column has freuqntly filter operation over the time.\n  - bucketing: bucketing is another techniqu to devide the data into mutlitple directory, but this is most suitable when we want to parition a data on the column where we have high cardinality and control the no of directory created.",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
